                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "239345106",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198162378642",
                            "num_reviews": 269,
                            "playtime_forever": 3905,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 1337,
                            "playtime_at_review": 3905,
                            "deck_playtime_at_review": 16,
                            "last_played": 1793787266
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game holds a special place for me because I played the original on the DS for a ridiculous number of hours when I was little. \r\n\r\nThe story hasn't aged too well for me and it's one of the game's weak spots. It's clearly a step down from FF II and you can tell the dev team was more interested in building the job system than in writing a memorable plot. I won't hold that against them since this job system became one of the pillars of the whole series. It's just that the conversations feel so NPC-like it's actually pretty funny.\r\n\r\nWhat I've always loved the most about this game is the characters and job outfits design, they are TOO CUTE. There's also a huge roster of characters, bosses, enemies and weapon that anyone who's followed the series will recognize right away.\r\n\r\n🪶 Check my reviews here → [url=https://liljatherobin.blogspot.com/]Lilja the Robin[/url]\r\n",
